  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "Evidence: Both completed experiments (config_004, config_031) are multimodal singleprofile with scvi_n200 and concat fusion, achieving ~53.2-53.6% accuracy. The image encoder choice (resnet50 vs vit_l) shows negligible difference, so that axis is largely resolved. The major unexplored axis is multiprofile aggregation, which could substantially change how cellular profiles are combined. This experiment (config_011) is the minimal logical extension of our best result (config_004): it adds multiprofile with avgpool aggregation while keeping scvi_n200, resnet50, and concat fusion fixed, isolating the effect of profile aggregation. This is the best use of experiment 3 because resolving whether multiprofile helps (and by how much) will determine whether to invest remaining budget in multiprofile+transformer variants or stay in singleprofile space. Expected cost: ~0.7-0.8 GPU hours (multiprofile data loading and avgpool aggregation add moderate overhead over the 0.56h singleprofile baseline, but avgpool is far cheaper than transformer aggregation)."
}

